# Kit maintainer (this repo only)

This file is **not** `crav1-*` so a folder dump of the library can omit it. Product repos get `.cursor/rules/crav1.mdc` (Cursor) or `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code), not this file.

This repo’s custom library uses the **`crav1`** prefix so it is distinct from Cursor built-ins. Skill and agent names stay the same on Claude Code.

There are **three install trees**. Cursor drop-in `.cursor/` is the source of the playbooks. `plugins/crav1/` is the Cursor plugin mirror. `.claude/` is the generated Claude Code drop-in. When you add or change a skill, agent, template, or kit rule, edit `.cursor/` and run `scripts/sync-crav1-plugin.sh`. That refreshes the plugin mirror and regenerates `.claude/`. Do not hand-edit mirrored files under `plugins/crav1/` or anything under `.claude/`. Also update `docs/install.md` and `plugins/crav1/README.md` when how people install or start using the kit changes.

CI (`.github/workflows/drop-in-plugin-sync.yml`) fails the check when the plugin mirror drifts, when `scripts/sync-crav1-claude.sh --check` exits non-zero because the committed `.claude/` tree does not match a fresh generate, when `scripts/gen-skill-docs.py --check` finds the skills reference out of line with `docs/reference/skills.yaml`, and when `scripts/check-kit-docs.py` finds a description over 1,024 characters or a `plugin.json` version that differs from the newest `CHANGELOG.md` release. A comment in this rule is not the check.

## Drop-in (project `.cursor/`)

- Skills: `.cursor/skills/crav1/crav1-<short-name>/` with frontmatter `name: crav1-<short-name>` (must match the folder that contains `SKILL.md`). Slash command: `/crav1-<short-name>`. Type `/crav1` to list them.
- Cross-cutting pull-request skills: `/crav1-open-pr` opens one pull request and does not merge. `/crav1-merge-pr` merges one named pull request only when the user explicitly asks in that turn, and only with a merge commit. Do not fold merge into open-pr, build-tasks, or review skills.
- Agents: `.cursor/agents/crav1-<name>.md` with `name: crav1-<name>`. Subagent `name:` ends in `-agent` so the Cursor slash picker can tell them apart from skills that share the same stem (`/crav1-review-architecture` stays the skill; `crav1-review-architecture-agent` is the subagent).
- Guild routing: when you add, rename, or remove a skill, agent, or cross-cutting helper, update `docs/guild-routing.md` in the same PR. Update `docs/reference/skills.yaml` in that same PR and run `scripts/gen-skill-docs.py` (see Skill reference below).
- Agent templates: `.cursor/agent-assets/crav1-<name>/` (not under `.cursor/agents/`).
- Usage rule for consuming repos: `.cursor/rules/crav1.mdc`. Keep it to standing rules that hold for every skill, plus pointers to the skills reference. Per-skill behavior belongs in that skill's `SKILL.md` and its `skills.yaml` entry, not in this rule.

Do not add unprefixed copies at `.cursor/skills/<short-name>/` (name collision).

## Plugin mirror (`plugins/crav1/`)

Cursor plugin layout (install-from-repo / local plugin):

- Manifest: `plugins/crav1/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`
- Catalog: `.cursor-plugin/marketplace.json` (repo root)
- Skills: `plugins/crav1/skills/crav1-<short-name>/` (same `name:` and `SKILL.md` as drop-in)
- Agents: `plugins/crav1/agents/crav1-<name>.md`
- Agent templates: `plugins/crav1/agent-assets/crav1-<name>/`
- Rules: `plugins/crav1/rules/` (includes `crav1.mdc`; do not put this maintainer file in the plugin)

After editing drop-in files, run `scripts/sync-crav1-plugin.sh` so the plugin tree and `.claude/` match. Do not hand-edit mirrored files only under `plugins/crav1/` or `.claude/` — they will be overwritten. Plugin-only files: `plugins/crav1/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`, `plugins/crav1/README.md`. The `version` in `plugin.json` follows the release tag: a release pull request sets it to the same number as its new `## X.Y.Z` heading in `CHANGELOG.md`. There is no Claude Code plugin marketplace in this kit.

## Claude Code drop-in (generated `.claude/`)

`scripts/sync-crav1-plugin.sh` calls `scripts/sync-crav1-claude.sh`, which writes `.claude/` from `.cursor/`. `scripts/sync-crav1-claude.sh --check` diffs a fresh generate against the committed tree and exits non-zero on drift. The same check runs in CI.

Path rewrite only: `.cursor/skills/crav1/<name>/` → `.claude/skills/<name>/`, `.cursor/agents/` → `.claude/agents/`, `.cursor/agent-assets/` → `.claude/agent-assets/`. Commit-style rules rewrite `.cursor/rules/draft-commit-*.mdc` to `.claude/rules/draft-commit-*.md`. The transfer data policy rewrites `.cursor/rules/crav1-transfer-data-policy.mdc` to `.claude/rules/crav1-transfer-data-policy.md`. The source skill text names Cursor and Claude Code; the generator rewrites the Cursor paths in the Claude copy.

Hand-written host differences inside that generator, not a second copy of every `SKILL.md`:

- Agent frontmatter. `model: inherit` is omitted (Claude Code’s default). `readonly: true` becomes `tools: Read, Grep, Glob`. Writers omit `tools` so they can edit.
- `.cursor/rules/crav1.mdc` becomes `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (the always-on project instruction, not the README).
- Commit-style assets drop Cursor `alwaysApply` frontmatter so `.claude/rules/*.md` loads at session start. The transfer data policy asset in `crav1-add-to-spec` gets the same drop.

`.claude/agent-assets/` is not a directory Claude Code loads on its own. Prompts read those files. Do not put them under `.claude/agents/` (that tree is scanned as subagents). Do not copy this maintainer file into `.claude/`.

## Self-contained templates

When you **create or update** a crav1 skill or subagent that reads or writes spec artifacts (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `adr.md`, `diagrams.md`, `verify.md`, `fix-log.md`) or landscape artifacts (`docs/system/`):

1. Put a copy of each template in **that skill’s** `assets/` (and the matching `agent-assets/crav1-<agent-name>/` on both trees).
2. Point the `SKILL.md` / agent prompt at **those** copies, not only `docs/specs/_template/`. Mention drop-in `.cursor/…` **and** plugin sibling paths when a file lives outside this skill. The Claude generator rewrites the `.cursor/` paths.
3. Keep `docs/specs/_template/` and `docs/system/_template/` in sync with the matching `assets/` copies. If you change a template, update **every** copy. Note files use `docs/notes/_template/note.md` and `docs/notes/_template/index.md`. The same two files live in `crav1-add-to-spec` `assets/`.
4. Do **not** put template markdown under `.cursor/agents/` or `plugins/crav1/agents/` except the agent prompt file.
5. Format recipes live in the skill’s `references/` (see `crav1-export-spec` / `crav1-ideas-to-spec`).

Skills that do not use those files do not need empty `assets/` folders.

Optional Azure Boards id file: `docs/specs/_template/work-item.md` is the HTML-comment starter only. Do not copy that template into skill `assets/`, and do not copy the comment into a slug. Commit and pull-request skills read `docs/specs/<slug>/work-item.md` when it exists. The file holds one id per line, with a milestone or slice label when one is recorded. A single unlabeled line is the old format and is still read. The mention picks the line whose label matches the slice being worked, and asks when that is unclear. `/crav1-spark-to-spec`, `/crav1-ideas-to-spec`, and `/crav1-bundle-to-specs` may write a line when the user opts in on Azure Repos (`crav1-finalize-commit` `references/work-item-offer.md`). They do not write the file when the user skips. Creating a Feature is `/crav1-ado-sync`.

## Install docs

Pre-install: `docs/install.md`. Post-plugin-install: `plugins/crav1/README.md`. Landing page: `README.md`. Docs index: `docs/README.md` (add every new page there). Method: `docs/concepts/method.md`. Data layout, glossary, and data policy: `docs/concepts/`. Walkthroughs: `docs/from-*.md`.

## Skill reference (behavior)

The behavior of every skill and subagent on main lives in the user-facing reference, not in this file: [`docs/reference/skills.md`](../../docs/reference/skills.md) (the table, grouped by lane) and `docs/reference/skills/crav1-<name>.md` (one page per skill: what it reads, writes, leaves alone, who calls it, and what it calls, plus its exceptions). Read that page before answering how a skill behaves. Lane ownership stays in `docs/guild-routing.md`.

Both are generated from one data file, `docs/reference/skills.yaml`. Do not hand-edit the generated pages.

- A new skill or subagent adds its entry to `skills.yaml` in the same pull request, then run `scripts/gen-skill-docs.py` and commit the regenerated pages.
- A change to what a skill reads, writes, leaves alone, calls, or names as the next step updates its `skills.yaml` entry in that same pull request, then regenerate.
- A rename or removal updates `skills.yaml`, `docs/guild-routing.md`, and the generated pages together. A rename also leaves an alias: a stub `SKILL.md` under the old name (`disable-model-invocation: true`, hands off to the new skill, passes its choice word), listed under `aliases` in `skills.yaml` with `deprecated: true` and `remove_in`. Aliases stay two releases and go in a breaking release; the 1.56.0 aliases go in 1.58.0.
- A merged skill keeps each old skill's rules verbatim in `branches/<id>/BRANCH.md` and opens with a question with options, with exact `choice_words` (no --flags). Do not drop a rule when merging.

A skill change is done only when it is documented, for a new skill and for a change to an existing skill.

A new skill is done only when it is documented: its `skills.yaml` entry and generated reference page, a walkthrough (its own `docs/from-*.md` page, or a step in a goal walkthrough such as `docs/from-draft-spec.md`) that links back to the reference page and is set as the entry's `walkthrough`, a line in `docs/README.md` when the walkthrough is new, and a `CHANGELOG.md` entry. A single-shot command may stay reference only (`walkthrough: null`) when the pull request says why.

A change to an existing skill is done only when the same pull request updates that skill's walkthrough (its `walkthrough` in `skills.yaml`) and, when the change adds or changes a word, a file, a column, or a mark, its entries in `docs/concepts/glossary.md` and `docs/concepts/data-layout.md`. A walkthrough that lands one pull request later is a gap, not done.

The order of commands lives only in `docs/reference/workflow.yaml`. It generates `docs/reference/workflow.md`, the order block in `crav1.mdc` (between the `crav1-order` markers), and every `you_run_next` in `skills.yaml`; run `scripts/gen-workflow.py`, then `scripts/gen-skill-docs.py` and `scripts/sync-crav1-plugin.sh`. Never hand-edit those three. The `/crav1-help` rule in `crav1.mdc` stays in all copies. Every install bundles `docs/` and `CHANGELOG.md` as `crav1-docs/` next to the skills (`.cursor/skills/crav1/crav1-docs/`, `plugins/crav1/skills/crav1-docs/`, `.claude/skills/crav1-docs/`), so each release answers for its own version. Never hand-edit `crav1-docs/`; run `scripts/sync-crav1-plugin.sh`.

CI fails when a generated page is stale, a skill folder or subagent is missing from `skills.yaml`, a lane in `skills.yaml` differs from the guild-routing map, a skill description is longer than 1,024 characters, or `plugins/crav1/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json` differs from the newest release heading in `CHANGELOG.md`. `scripts/gen-workflow.py --check` fails on route, `you_run_next`, order-block, help-rule, or walkthrough `## After` drift, and the sync job fails when any `crav1-docs/` copy differs from `docs/`. `scripts/check-skill-docs-touched.py` (workflow `skill-docs-touched.yml`) fails a pull request that changes any copy of a `SKILL.md` when no change under `docs/` outside `docs/reference/` covers that skill: its walkthrough, or a changed line naming it. Opt out only when the change needs no docs, with the `docs-not-needed` label or a `Docs-not-needed: <reason>` line in the pull request body.
